2:08:35 PM [express] POST /api/ai/chat 200 in 91622ms :: {"response":"Here's a sample Indian diet plan focusing on weight loss principles suitable for someone who enjoys Indian cuisine:\n\n## 🌅 Breakfast\n**~400 kcal | 20g | 50g | 10g**\n*   Upma made with semolina (rava) and vegetable broth instead of onion and garlic.  Use less oil than traditional recipes. (~200kcal, 8gP, 30gC, 3gF)\n*   Boiled Egg White: 1 large (~70kcal, 6gP, 1gC, 5gF)\n*   Small serving of mixed sprouts salad (~30kcal, 2gP, 5gC, 0gF)\n\n## 🍎 Mid-Morning Snack\n**~150 kcal | 8g | 15g | 5g**\n*   Roasted Chana Masala (chickpeas) prepared with very little oil and spices. (~150kcal, 8gP, 15gC, 5gF)\n\n## 🍽️ Lunch\n**~600 kcal | 35g | 70g | 20g**\n*   Dal Makhani (prepared with reduced cream and butter) served with Brown Rice (~450kcal, 25gP, 60gC, 10gF)\n*   Mixed Vegetable Sabzi (low-oil stir fry with lots of veggies) (~150kcal, 10gP, 20gC, 5gF)\n\n## 🌆 Evening Snack\n**~150 kcal | 5g | 20g | 8g**\n*   Moong Dal Cheela (lentil pancake) made with whole wheat flour and limited oil. Serve with yogurt dip (~150kcal, 5gP, 20gC, 8gF)\n\n## 🌙 Dinner\n**~500 kcal | 30g | 40g | 20g**\n*   Grilled Fish Kabab (boneless pieces marinated in ginger-garlic paste and spices) served with steamed green beans (~400kcal, 25gP, 40gC, 10gF)\n*   Roti (whole wheat flatbread) made with minimal oil (~100kcal, 5gP, 10gC, 2gF)\n\n## ⚠️ Foods to Avoid\n*   Deep Fried Snacks (pakoras, samosas)\n*   Rich Creamy Curries (excessively creamy gravies)\n*   Large Portions of Bread Items (naan, paratha)\n*   Sugar Sweetened Drinks (colas, sugary sodas)\n*   Overly Processed Ready-to-Eat Foods\n\n## 💡 Why This Plan\nThis plan incorporates several key elements for effective weight loss:\n\n*   **Reduced Calorie Intake:** Portion sizes are controlled across all meals, aiming for approximately 1200-1500 calories per day, adjusting according to activity levels and metabolism.\n*   **Increased Fiber:** Emphasis on whole grains (brown rice, roti), lentils (dal), and vegetables provides sustained energy release and promotes fullness.\n*   **Lean Proteins:** Chicken, fish, and dals offer valuable amino acids crucial for maintaining muscle mass during weight loss.\n*   **Healthy Fats:** Incorporating small quantities of nuts, seeds, and oils derived from olives or mustard reduces unhealthy fat intake.\n*   **Limited Refined Carbohydrates:** Reducing reliance on white bread, sweets, and processed carbohydrates minimizes rapid spikes in blood sugar.\n*   **Portion Control:** Serving sizes are carefully managed to prevent overeating.\n*   **Hydration:** Drinking plenty of water aids digestion, boosts metabolism, and suppresses appetite.\n\nRemember to consult with a registered dietitian or healthcare professional for personalized guidance and support. They can assess your unique nutritional requirements and develop a sustainable eating strategy aligned with your goals.","followUpQuestions":[]}
